# Database safety

Schema reference: `ai/DATABASE.md`.

- Schema changes only via a new Flyway file `V{n+1}__name.sql`; never edit an applied migration.
- Never drop, truncate, reset or bulk-delete in `RagDB` (dev DB with real data) without explicit user approval.
- Do not run migrations or seeds against a shared or production DB automatically; verify the target DB first
  (seed scripts must refuse non-localhost targets).
- Seeds must be deterministic and idempotent (match existing rows by slug/SKU, never duplicate).
- Prefer a scratch DB (e.g. `ragdb_catalog_check`) or Testcontainers for verification.
- Never print or store `DB_PASSWORD` or other `.env` values in output, docs or code.
- Update `ai/DATABASE.md` after any schema or seed change.
